 "cacheBoundary": {
  "cache_key(domain,key)": "PURE deterministic key construction: exact schema admission and canonical order only. Reads no bytes, resolves no reference, grants nothing. A host may compute it before loading anything and miss cheaply.",
  "admit_cache_entry(domain,key,run,objects,blobs)": "POST-CONSTRUCTION conformance check over an ADMITTED Run. Not the pre-analysis cache scheduling API; no Run is required to consume an intermediate hit and there is no dependency cycle. A host schedules with cache_key, provisionally loads producer bytes, and those bytes then face ordinary stage and closure admission before any Run authority.",
  "checks": [
   "stage must be one the execution plan carries",
   "stage spec joins this Plan",
   "producer closure retained and Plan-selected",
   "every scopeIds member a retained subject-scope of this snapshot",
   "output schema document retained",
   "every inputRefs entry dispatched through the same x-opensip-digest-domains registry the Run uses",
   "consumed native context must be Plan-selected; consumed import must be Plan-selected",
   "bare coverage-payload/import-payload/fact-payload refs refused as authoritative roots (no guessed schema)"
  ],
  "doesNotDo": [
   "model a miss (a miss is not a failure; the host recomputes)",
   "fetch or validate the cached OUTPUT bytes",
   "decide reuse policy"
  ],
  "notClaimed": "This is not a complete cache subsystem and is not claimed to be full cache HIT validation.",
  "foreignObjectHypothesis": "ASSESSED, not assumed. visit() already applies REFERENCE_PLAN_JOIN and REFERENCE_SOURCE_JOIN to objects first reached through a cache reference. Negatives added anyway: a self-consistent foreign view refuses REFERENCE_PLAN_JOIN and a foreign scope refuses CACHE_SCOPE_SOURCE_JOIN, from a mixed store, with a control that the Run's own view still admits."
 },
